From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] osk: The microphone key shows what dictation does

While dictating the key was only lit in the accent color, so nothing
told whether the model was still loading, whether the microphone heard
anything, or whether text was on its way after a pause.

plinius-dictate 0.2 sends what it does (Activity: loading, listening,
speech, recognizing, idle) and the loudness of the microphone (Level,
about 15 times a second). The key animates for it, over its icon:

- a ring that breathes calmly while the microphone is open and grows
  with the voice, rising quickly and falling slowly like a level meter,
- an arc that turns while the model loads or spoken text is being
  recognized, also after the microphone was switched off until the last
  words arrived.

The arc starts at once on a tap, as activating the service takes a
moment. The animation runs at most 30 times a second and redraws only
the key; drawing skips the keys outside of the redrawn area.
